id:                     E14858
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|conan
phase:                  configuration|testing
error_signature:        set_property could not find TARGET|upstream test binary exists but CTest does not register it|CTest testlo bind Operation not permitted under inherited TMPDIR
severity:               2
category:               cmake,build-system,test,ohos
match_keywords:         CMake target creation order,CTest inventory,unregistered test,C++ exception variant,network fixture,Conan environment activation,TMPDIR socket capability
title:                  Audit CMake test targets against CTest registration before claiming full upstream coverage
root_cause:             A project can configure target properties before add_library creates the target, and can build a test variant without add_test registration; a green ctest then covers only the registered subset.
affected_scope:         CMake projects with optional test variants, CTest registration, or test targets whose properties are set before target creation.
verification_cmd:       Compare source test targets and built test executables with ctest -N, then execute ctest --output-on-failure and require exact N/N with zero skipped tests.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           repair-target-order-and-complete-registration
rec_description:        Move target properties after creation and register missing variants. Preserve network assertions with bounded waits. For AF_UNIX tests use a unique short native application-private files directory and set TMPDIR in the command after Conan activation; writable cache paths are not proof of bind capability. Clean the owned directory after CTest even on failure.
rec_command:            cmake -S <source> -B <build> -DWITH_TESTS=ON -DWITH_CPP_TESTS=ON; cmake --build <build>; ctest --test-dir <build> -N; ctest --test-dir <build> --output-on-failure
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-test-registration-patch
forbid_1_pattern:       count-only-registered-tests
forbid_1_reason:        CTest cannot report tests never registered, so its 100 percent summary alone does not prove the upstream inventory is complete.
forbid_1_consequence:   Missing upstream variants are silently omitted from the declared denominator.
principles:             []
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E605]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E14858-draft-2501.md
last_updated:           2026-10-10
source_event:           CI 80115 testlo bind EPERM under cache TMPDIR with other 3/4 CTests passing; repaired liblo/0.32 W3 liblo-w3-20261010T103000Z CTest 4/4 plus installed consumer 1/1 and 12 receipts; raw log SHA-256 56f891d5db81336e327b3bf329c7379ca0545d3fd60ba2c71b6e6b69cf64c9a6.
metrics_success_count:  1
